   "title": "Personnel Recovery",
   "html": "<blockquote class=\"quote\"><p>The various CAS controllers occupy a unique location in the operational area, which may allow them to be the first asset to realize that a personnel recovery isolating event has occurred. They should be prepared to assume on-scene commander (OSC) duties to report the event to higher authorities, locate the isolated personnel, and support them as necessary until relieved by another OSC or a rescue mission commander.</p><p>See JP 3-50, Personnel Recovery, for additional instructions and guidance.</p><cite>JP 3-09.3, p. I-11</cite></blockquote>",
